1
00:00:04,140 --> 00:00:05,900
Why is it snowing?

2
00:00:05,900 --> 00:00:07,230
Emilia-sama!

3
00:00:11,190 --> 00:00:13,320
Everyone! What happened?

4
00:00:13,320 --> 00:00:14,520
Why is it snowing?

5
00:00:14,860 --> 00:00:17,450
It only started falling moments ago,

6
00:00:17,450 --> 00:00:19,870
and it's already accumulated this much.

7
00:00:20,370 --> 00:00:22,540
And of course, we can't evacuate.

8
00:00:22,540 --> 00:00:25,220
We've escaped it thanks to this, but...

9
00:00:25,220 --> 00:00:27,580
Who made this for you?

10
00:00:30,210 --> 00:00:33,210
It wasn't you, Emilia-sama?

11
00:00:33,210 --> 00:00:35,010
What? Me?

12
00:00:35,630 --> 00:00:36,690
No...

13
00:00:36,690 --> 00:00:40,810
But that spirit said if we 
wanted to thank someone,

14
00:00:40,810 --> 00:00:43,100
We should thank Emilia-sama... 
rather, "Lia."

15
00:00:44,270 --> 00:00:45,230
Puck...

16
00:01:02,370 --> 00:01:05,620
<i>You still have a job to do, don't you, Lia?</i>

17
00:01:08,330 --> 00:01:10,840
Everyone, I've finished the trial.

18
00:01:11,250 --> 00:01:14,380
But I think it'll be too 
dangerous to move now.

19
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:17,550
So take refuge in the graveyard.

20
00:01:17,550 --> 00:01:18,260
You...

21
00:01:19,220 --> 00:01:20,720
Can I count on you to handle this?

22
00:01:22,140 --> 00:01:22,770
Yes!

23
00:01:23,020 --> 00:01:25,600
What will you do, Emilia-sama?

24
00:01:26,440 --> 00:01:29,560
It seems like I have to go over there.

25
00:01:30,810 --> 00:01:32,360
Can you stay safe and wait for me?

26
00:01:35,320 --> 00:01:38,660
We will keep the promise we made 
before you started the trial.

27
00:01:38,660 --> 00:01:41,530
Please stay safe yourself, Emilia-sama.

28
00:01:58,220 --> 00:01:59,090
Ram...

29
00:02:00,180 --> 00:02:02,640
You lost your temper when 
she burned the book.

30
00:02:03,390 --> 00:02:04,640
That's not like you...

31
00:02:05,220 --> 00:02:07,310
But she was prepared for what would happen.

32
00:02:07,810 --> 00:02:09,060
She is strong.

33
00:02:11,190 --> 00:02:14,860
Ram... Why did you...

34
00:02:15,820 --> 00:02:20,160
Roswaal-sama, I love you.

35
00:02:20,360 --> 00:02:22,780
You've lost, Roswaal.

36
00:02:23,370 --> 00:02:25,370
She achieved her goal.

37
00:02:26,160 --> 00:02:28,160
She crossed that fine line.

38
00:02:29,750 --> 00:02:32,130
Soon, Lia will complete her trial.

39
00:02:32,420 --> 00:02:34,290
And the book you relied on is gone.

40
00:02:34,880 --> 00:02:38,720
Your attachment to it was impressive, but...

41
00:02:41,140 --> 00:02:42,180
Snow?

42
00:02:42,340 --> 00:02:43,680
It can't be!

43
00:02:46,520 --> 00:02:52,440
You got me. You inscribed the spell that calls
the snow clouds before the battle began?

44
00:02:53,810 --> 00:02:55,150
The snow will fall.

45
00:02:55,440 --> 00:02:57,820
It'll turn out just as Subaru feared.

46
00:02:58,690 --> 00:03:00,740
I'm going to go try to delay that.

47
00:03:03,620 --> 00:03:06,120
Roswaal, you amaze me.

48
00:03:06,120 --> 00:03:07,830
You're quite the magician.

49
00:03:08,540 --> 00:03:12,670
As far as I know, there's no 
human alive as skilled as you.

50
00:03:14,170 --> 00:03:17,800
But no matter how far you go,
you're still a human.

51
00:03:18,170 --> 00:03:20,130
You'll never be like that devil.

52
00:03:43,110 --> 00:03:47,120
I made snow fall, as the 
Tome of Wisdom dictated.

53
00:03:50,160 --> 00:03:51,870
What do I do now?

54
00:04:05,590 --> 00:04:06,470
Ram...

55
00:04:08,060 --> 00:04:10,270
Yes, that's it, Ram...

56
00:04:19,190 --> 00:04:21,940
Teacher, what shall I...

57
00:04:23,450 --> 00:04:30,370
What shall I... What am I 
supposed to do, Teacher?!

58
00:04:32,120 --> 00:04:35,580
I don't... I still don't know anything.

59
00:04:36,540 --> 00:04:39,750
So give me your guidance again, Teacher...

60
00:04:47,970 --> 00:04:49,470
Mana is swirling here.

61
00:04:50,310 --> 00:04:53,350
Is this what's making the snow fall?

62
00:05:00,400 --> 00:05:02,860
Puck is waiting. I have to go.

63
00:05:09,120 --> 00:05:10,240
Ryuzu-san?

64
00:05:11,330 --> 00:05:13,900
Emilia-sama? Why are you here?

65
00:05:16,710 --> 00:05:18,290
This many of you?

66
00:05:19,210 --> 00:05:23,060
That must've been really 
rough on your mother.

67
00:05:23,060 --> 00:05:26,220
Explanations about us clones can wait.

68
00:05:26,220 --> 00:05:28,760
Please, for now, just stop me!

69
00:05:28,760 --> 00:05:30,600
Stop... you?

70
00:05:35,480 --> 00:05:37,270
You're Shima-san, right?

71
00:05:37,810 --> 00:05:41,270
The fact that you are here, Emilia-sama,

72
00:05:41,270 --> 00:05:43,610
must mean that you have overcome the trial.

73
00:05:44,190 --> 00:05:46,610
Young Gar's wager was correct.

74
00:05:47,400 --> 00:05:50,370
Is that Ryuzu-san inside the magic crystal?

75
00:05:50,370 --> 00:05:52,120
Are you here to get her out?

76
00:05:52,620 --> 00:05:54,830
Should we all take her to 
the graveyard together?

77
00:05:55,830 --> 00:05:57,370
<i>Unbelievable.</i>

78
00:05:57,370 --> 00:06:00,750
<i>You see this, and that's the 
first thing you think of?</i>

79
00:06:01,420 --> 00:06:03,340
Yes, it'll be fine.

80
00:06:03,340 --> 00:06:05,670
If we make a sled and put her on it,

81
00:06:05,670 --> 00:06:07,680
I think we can all pull her there.

82
00:06:08,880 --> 00:06:11,020
We do appreciate it,

83
00:06:11,020 --> 00:06:15,890
but the reason I came here 
is to fulfill my role,

84
00:06:15,890 --> 00:06:18,520
along with my progenitor, 
who sleeps within this crystal.

85
00:06:18,520 --> 00:06:20,020
Fulfill your role?

86
00:06:20,230 --> 00:06:25,030
This crystal is the core of the 
barrier surrounding the Sanctuary.

87
00:06:25,030 --> 00:06:27,950
You undid its spell, Emilia-sama.

88
00:06:27,950 --> 00:06:30,320
Now, once the core is gone,

89
00:06:30,320 --> 00:06:33,990
the Sanctuary's role will be completed, 
and it will be liberated.

90
00:06:34,990 --> 00:06:36,950
<i>If</i> it is gone, that is.

91
00:06:37,200 --> 00:06:41,080
Um... Does that have to happen right now?

92
00:06:41,080 --> 00:06:43,500
It's snowing really hard outside...

93
00:06:43,500 --> 00:06:48,010
In the event that this facility is destroyed 
and the one who runs it is lost,

94
00:06:48,010 --> 00:06:50,630
the resulting damage will be irreparable.

95
00:06:50,630 --> 00:06:53,250
We are the key to preventing that.

96
00:07:00,850 --> 00:07:03,060
Emilia-sama, take this.

97
00:07:06,190 --> 00:07:08,570
Wait! Is this Puck?

98
00:07:08,570 --> 00:07:11,950
The great spirit visited here in advance

99
00:07:11,950 --> 00:07:14,410
and delayed the spell's activation.

100
00:07:14,410 --> 00:07:19,200
He exhausted all of his 
strength to save everyone.

101
00:07:19,200 --> 00:07:24,000
He made that wall of ice to 
protect everyone from the snow,

102
00:07:24,790 --> 00:07:27,840
and pushed himself this 
far to let me know.

103
00:07:28,460 --> 00:07:31,590
How many other impossible tasks did you do?

104
00:07:32,090 --> 00:07:34,890
He lent us aid in many forms.

105
00:07:34,890 --> 00:07:39,010
Now that we have been 
given this opportunity,

106
00:07:39,560 --> 00:07:43,010
it is my responsibility 
to fulfill our role.

107
00:07:43,770 --> 00:07:45,780
I understand your role, but—

108
00:07:45,780 --> 00:07:50,150
Our beloved grandson has 
been with me for ten years.

109
00:07:50,150 --> 00:07:55,990
Garf, our grandson, is giving his 
all to make it to the outside.

110
00:07:55,990 --> 00:07:59,160
I will give him a push.

111
00:07:59,620 --> 00:08:02,540
Please watch and see where it takes him,

112
00:08:02,920 --> 00:08:06,090
my sisters made from half of me.

113
00:08:16,970 --> 00:08:19,260
I'll take care of the rest.

114
00:08:21,980 --> 00:08:25,900
You have grown a shocking 
amount in only half a day.

115
00:08:25,900 --> 00:08:29,280
This is the one thing old folks 
such as me take pleasure in.

116
00:08:56,590 --> 00:08:58,180
Let's go, Ryuzu-san.

117
00:08:58,930 --> 00:09:01,770
There's something we need to do.

118
00:09:02,140 --> 00:09:03,640
Emilia-sama...

119
00:09:04,600 --> 00:09:06,350
A desire has been entrusted to me,

120
00:09:06,900 --> 00:09:08,690
and I have a wish I want to fulfill.

121
00:09:09,730 --> 00:09:11,900
So crying and all that can wait.

122
00:09:12,360 --> 00:09:15,820
That's what the people I love 
told me, always with a smile.

123
00:09:19,830 --> 00:09:24,000
Please, tell me where Ram and Roswaal are.

124
00:09:38,050 --> 00:09:39,680
Ram! Roswaal!

125
00:09:44,980 --> 00:09:48,190
Come on, Roswaal! You can't stay here!

126
00:09:48,190 --> 00:09:49,810
You can't freeze solid!

127
00:09:55,780 --> 00:09:56,530
Ram?

128
00:09:57,610 --> 00:09:59,620
Ram? Ram!

129
00:10:03,290 --> 00:10:03,870
She's alive!

130
00:10:04,290 --> 00:10:07,410
It's all right. There's still time! Roswaal!

131
00:10:09,540 --> 00:10:11,170
You're helping Ram, right?

132
00:10:12,090 --> 00:10:15,300
Roswaal, just bring Ram and come with me.

133
00:10:15,300 --> 00:10:17,380
I'll do what I can, so don't give u—

134
00:10:17,380 --> 00:10:18,930
It doesn't matter.

135
00:10:19,260 --> 00:10:19,890
Huh?

136
00:10:20,840 --> 00:10:22,300
It doesn't matter anymore.

137
00:10:25,310 --> 00:10:27,560
Don't say things like that!

138
00:10:27,560 --> 00:10:30,020
What do you mean, it doesn't matter anymore?

139
00:10:30,020 --> 00:10:32,230
Of course it still matters!

140
00:10:32,230 --> 00:10:35,230
Don't just give up and 
accept that it's over!

141
00:10:35,230 --> 00:10:37,610
For me, for Ram, and for you...

142
00:10:37,610 --> 00:10:40,740
There's not a single thing 
that doesn't matter anymore!

143
00:10:41,120 --> 00:10:43,110
I completed the trial!

144
00:10:43,580 --> 00:10:45,490
The past that I was afraid to face,

145
00:10:45,490 --> 00:10:47,750
the happy present that could have happened,

146
00:10:47,750 --> 00:10:50,120
the tragic future that might come one day...

147
00:10:50,120 --> 00:10:51,380
I saw it all!

148
00:10:51,380 --> 00:10:55,210
I saw it and still made up 
my mind to walk this path!

149
00:10:55,210 --> 00:10:57,590
And now I finally get to start walking!

150
00:11:02,760 --> 00:11:04,640
When you're talking with someone,

151
00:11:04,640 --> 00:11:07,480
you need to look them in the face!

152
00:11:09,350 --> 00:11:12,310
I won't let anyone say it 
doesn't matter anymore.

153
00:11:12,310 --> 00:11:16,030
As long as you're alive, there's nothing
 that doesn't matter anymore.

154
00:11:16,400 --> 00:11:21,110
So I'm never going to 
give up on anyone again!

155
00:11:28,950 --> 00:11:30,040
They're following me.

156
00:11:30,460 --> 00:11:32,960
Right... because I'm a witch.

157
00:11:33,580 --> 00:11:36,420
Or is it because Puck is with me?

158
00:11:44,680 --> 00:11:46,180
Take Roswaal and Ram.

159
00:11:50,060 --> 00:11:51,890
When we get back to the graveyard,

160
00:11:51,890 --> 00:11:54,150
I will protect all of you!

161
00:12:03,160 --> 00:12:06,080
<i>I first began waiting for "that person"</i>

162
00:12:06,080 --> 00:12:07,870
<i>right after I lost Ryuzu,</i>

163
00:12:07,870 --> 00:12:13,870
<i>and the Sanctuary was 
established in her place.</i>

164
00:12:18,840 --> 00:12:24,050
Beatrice, I'm leaving you in charge of 
the library filled with my knowledge.

165
00:12:25,550 --> 00:12:31,850
I want you to continue protecting 
this library until the time comes.

166
00:12:31,850 --> 00:12:32,520
What?

167
00:12:33,060 --> 00:12:36,150
I know. We'll call it the forbidden library.

168
00:12:36,520 --> 00:12:42,030
I will write down all of the knowledge 
I possess and store it there.

169
00:12:42,030 --> 00:12:43,110
W-Wait...

170
00:12:43,110 --> 00:12:46,620
Build the library in Roswaal's mansion.

171
00:12:46,620 --> 00:12:49,370
I'm sure he will help you.

172
00:12:49,370 --> 00:12:50,870
Wait, I suppose!

173
00:12:51,080 --> 00:12:54,580
Wh-What forbidden library? I don't 
know what you're talking about!

174
00:12:54,580 --> 00:12:56,210
I want to stay with you!

175
00:12:56,210 --> 00:13:01,090
I'm sorry, but you'll be of no help 
against an enemy Roswaal can't handle.

176
00:13:01,460 --> 00:13:03,970
If both you and I die,

177
00:13:03,970 --> 00:13:05,970
what becomes of that 
accumulation of knowledge?

178
00:13:05,970 --> 00:13:08,600
I am obligated to pass it down.

179
00:13:09,050 --> 00:13:13,640
You mean... my power exists...
 for this moment?

180
00:13:15,310 --> 00:13:18,020
You knew it all from the start?

181
00:13:22,740 --> 00:13:23,690
What is this?

182
00:13:23,990 --> 00:13:30,160
It is incomplete, but it's a replica of the 
Tome of Wisdom, the Authority granted to me.

183
00:13:30,580 --> 00:13:34,200
It should serve as a simple guide 
to its owner's future, at least.

184
00:13:35,660 --> 00:13:37,290
There are two copies of this book.

185
00:13:37,290 --> 00:13:41,210
This one is for you, and I 
gave the other to Roswaal.

186
00:13:41,590 --> 00:13:44,470
I'm sorry, but please understand.

187
00:13:45,380 --> 00:13:47,090
Let's discuss the time frame.

188
00:13:47,630 --> 00:13:50,010
If, for some reason, I don't return,

189
00:13:50,010 --> 00:13:55,020
someone suitable for inheriting 
my knowledge will come for you.

190
00:13:55,020 --> 00:13:56,850
Come... for me?

191
00:13:57,020 --> 00:13:59,940
For now, let's just call them "that person."

192
00:13:59,940 --> 00:14:04,190
Wait for that person. 
This is my last request.

193
00:14:07,320 --> 00:14:08,160
Betty...

194
00:14:09,530 --> 00:14:11,990
I want you to grow up healthy, at least.

195
00:14:18,620 --> 00:14:23,800
<i>As Mother instructed, I relocated 
to Roswaal's mansion,</i>

196
00:14:23,800 --> 00:14:27,050
<i>built the forbidden library, 
and became its librarian.</i>

197
00:14:27,800 --> 00:14:33,010
<i>At some point, Roswaal started visiting 
the forbidden library frequently.</i>

198
00:14:33,010 --> 00:14:37,020
Hello. I'm back for another visit today.

199
00:14:38,270 --> 00:14:41,110
Replicating a soul...

200
00:14:41,110 --> 00:14:44,270
<i>What he sought was within the books.</i>

201
00:14:41,690 --> 00:14:44,270
Saving it in a vessel...

202
00:14:44,270 --> 00:14:47,030
<i>We rarely spoke to each other at all.</i>

203
00:14:49,360 --> 00:14:51,620
Pleased to meet you, Beatrice-sama.

204
00:14:52,320 --> 00:14:56,110
I have heard about you from my predecessor.

205
00:14:57,410 --> 00:14:58,660
Do not worry.

206
00:14:59,160 --> 00:15:02,420
As the current Roswaal, Roswaal B. Mathers,

207
00:15:02,420 --> 00:15:06,770
I will inherit your role and 
your debt to your mother.

208
00:15:07,760 --> 00:15:11,800
<i>Control over the mansion was handed 
down throughout the Mathers clan</i>

209
00:15:11,800 --> 00:15:13,600
<i>from one Roswaal to the next.</i>

210
00:15:14,390 --> 00:15:19,560
<i>Nothing worth speaking of happened 
for 400 years after that.</i>

211
00:15:22,650 --> 00:15:25,770
<i>A few people found their way 
to the forbidden library</i>

212
00:15:25,770 --> 00:15:27,740
<i>and tried to take me out of it,</i>

213
00:15:28,410 --> 00:15:30,360
<i>but it never happened.</i>

214
00:15:31,360 --> 00:15:34,410
<i>When I was unexpectedly reunited with 
the one I admired as a big brother,</i>

215
00:15:34,410 --> 00:15:36,410
<i>my heart sang for the first time in ages.</i>

216
00:15:36,950 --> 00:15:38,780
<i>But I quickly realized that</i>

217
00:15:39,410 --> 00:15:41,140
<i>my brother and I weren't the same.</i>

218
00:15:41,870 --> 00:15:44,300
<i>Driven by envy and jealousy,</i>

219
00:15:44,300 --> 00:15:48,550
<i>I killed my emotions and stopped talking 
so I wouldn't hurt the half-devil girl</i>

220
00:15:48,550 --> 00:15:50,010
<i>who was always with him.</i>

221
00:15:51,630 --> 00:15:52,850
<i>And then...</i>

222
00:15:52,850 --> 00:15:54,510
NPC #1 found!

223
00:15:54,970 --> 00:15:58,970
<i>Suddenly, with no hesitation, an outsider 
walked in with his dirty shoes on.</i>

224
00:15:59,220 --> 00:15:59,880
Yo!

225
00:15:59,880 --> 00:16:02,270
<i>For whatever reason, 
he stayed in the mansion.</i>

226
00:16:00,270 --> 00:16:01,310
Beako!

227
00:16:01,310 --> 00:16:02,270
Beako!

228
00:16:02,810 --> 00:16:06,650
<i>He was somehow different from the others 
who had come to the forbidden library.</i>

229
00:16:06,650 --> 00:16:11,200
<i>At times, I even thought he might be 
"that person," as Mother had talked about.</i>

230
00:16:13,820 --> 00:16:17,400
<i>Afraid that the faint hope 
I had would end up betrayed,</i>

231
00:16:17,700 --> 00:16:21,830
<i>I sent him to the Sanctuary 
according to Roswaal's plans.</i>

232
00:16:22,750 --> 00:16:25,000
<i>Then Roswaal departed for the Sanctuary,</i>

233
00:16:25,630 --> 00:16:28,920
<i>saying he was off to see the Witch of Greed,</i>

234
00:16:28,920 --> 00:16:31,720
<i>and I realized he intended 
to settle the score.</i>

235
00:16:32,470 --> 00:16:33,840
<i>What about me, then?</i>

236
00:16:34,390 --> 00:16:38,510
<i>A blank book, a promised savior 
who never came for me...</i>

237
00:16:39,060 --> 00:16:40,430
<i>I finally realized</i>

238
00:16:40,930 --> 00:16:44,270
<i>"that person" was 
never going to show up.</i>

239
00:16:45,060 --> 00:16:47,150
<i>I've known that for a long time.</i>

240
00:16:47,440 --> 00:16:48,300
<i>And yet...</i>

241
00:16:48,300 --> 00:16:50,560
I'm getting you out of here, Beatrice.

242
00:16:51,110 --> 00:16:55,700
This time, you're gonna let me 
drag you out into the sunlight...

243
00:16:54,700 --> 00:17:01,200
Would you be... "that person" for me?

244
00:16:59,740 --> 00:17:01,200
Are you dumb?

245
00:17:01,200 --> 00:17:03,120
There's no way I could be whoever
 "that person" is—

246
00:17:06,380 --> 00:17:08,670
<i>I'm so tired.</i>

247
00:17:17,760 --> 00:17:20,260
Damn it! Where are you, Beako?!

248
00:17:37,280 --> 00:17:39,580
I might as well just...

249
00:17:39,950 --> 00:17:41,790
I finally made it back!

250
00:17:42,040 --> 00:17:43,500
Hey, you idiot! You've got some nerve—

251
00:17:43,500 --> 00:17:44,500
Belote!

252
00:17:46,710 --> 00:17:49,540
You're the one who ended our conversation.

253
00:17:49,750 --> 00:17:52,500
And now you... How impudent 
you are, I suppose.

254
00:17:52,960 --> 00:17:54,420
Cut that out already!

255
00:17:54,760 --> 00:17:56,510
You have the temper of a child!

256
00:17:56,510 --> 00:17:58,760
If you jump straight to 
violence, we'll never—

257
00:17:56,510 --> 00:17:58,760
<i>You</i> need to cut it out!

258
00:18:04,980 --> 00:18:06,640
I endured that one!

259
00:18:06,640 --> 00:18:07,980
You don't know when to give up!

260
00:18:08,310 --> 00:18:11,270
Until you actually shut me out for real,

261
00:18:11,270 --> 00:18:13,070
I'll just come back over and over!

262
00:18:13,730 --> 00:18:15,570
I am shutting you out for—

263
00:18:14,490 --> 00:18:17,570
No, you're not! If you were serious,

264
00:18:17,570 --> 00:18:20,240
would I be able to come 
back here so many times?!

265
00:18:20,240 --> 00:18:22,200
You're just putting on a front!

266
00:18:27,790 --> 00:18:32,040
You... You're not... "that person"!

267
00:18:32,460 --> 00:18:35,300
You said yourself that you're not!

268
00:18:35,300 --> 00:18:38,550
You said it! You did, I suppose!

269
00:18:39,010 --> 00:18:40,970
If you were "that person"...

270
00:18:41,510 --> 00:18:43,930
If you'd said you were, 
even if it was a lie,

271
00:18:43,930 --> 00:18:46,350
I know I would've believed you.

272
00:18:46,890 --> 00:18:50,020
Even knowing it was a lie, 
I would've had to believe you!

273
00:18:51,440 --> 00:18:52,820
Beatrice...

274
00:18:53,360 --> 00:18:56,740
But you said you weren't, I suppose!

275
00:18:57,320 --> 00:19:00,990
You said you weren't, and I was dumb!
 That's what you said!

276
00:19:00,990 --> 00:19:06,990
Because I'm a fool... a huge fool who 
can't forget a 400-year-old promise...

277
00:19:07,210 --> 00:19:11,290
So no matter what you say, 
it's over, I suppose!

278
00:19:18,600 --> 00:19:19,370
I'm...

279
00:19:23,650 --> 00:19:27,220
I'm not whoever "that person" is.

280
00:19:27,220 --> 00:19:28,890
I'll say it all you want!

281
00:19:30,990 --> 00:19:31,940
But...

282
00:19:34,320 --> 00:19:38,150
I want to stay with you, Beatrice.

283
00:19:40,250 --> 00:19:42,990
I want to be near you so you won't be sad,

284
00:19:43,620 --> 00:19:45,700
because you're a nice girl!

285
00:20:01,810 --> 00:20:03,090
What the...

286
00:20:12,240 --> 00:20:13,600
Beatrice!

287
00:20:18,240 --> 00:20:19,370
No!

288
00:20:28,500 --> 00:20:30,660
The entrance to the mansion...

289
00:20:30,660 --> 00:20:33,120
Is she telling me to just leave for good?

290
00:20:35,090 --> 00:20:37,800
If all the doors in the mansion burn down,

291
00:20:38,180 --> 00:20:40,210
her forbidden library will...

292
00:20:40,810 --> 00:20:42,020
Farewell.

293
00:20:42,430 --> 00:20:44,840
"Farewell," my ass!

294
00:20:44,840 --> 00:20:47,890
You think I'm just gonna 
let you end it like that?!

295
00:20:55,030 --> 00:20:57,270
There are no doors left...

296
00:21:00,990 --> 00:21:02,500
Yes, there are!

297
00:21:23,640 --> 00:21:27,680
Beatrice, if you can hear me, listen.

298
00:21:29,310 --> 00:21:31,600
There aren't any other doors left.

299
00:21:31,940 --> 00:21:34,210
This is the last one.

300
00:21:34,780 --> 00:21:38,360
If I open it, I'll probably die.

301
00:21:46,460 --> 00:21:47,990
Beatrice...

302
00:21:48,450 --> 00:21:50,910
I have faith in you!

303
00:22:03,600 --> 00:22:05,670
You are a fool.

304
00:22:05,980 --> 00:22:08,480
That's the first thing you say?

305
00:22:09,150 --> 00:22:10,970
Well, it's true, I suppose.

306
00:22:11,360 --> 00:22:13,770
It's a stalemate now.

307
00:22:15,030 --> 00:22:17,650
There is little more I could ask for now.

308
00:22:17,990 --> 00:22:21,850
My promise with Mother has been 
fully realized, I suppose.

309
00:22:22,620 --> 00:22:23,980
Then...

310
00:22:25,370 --> 00:22:28,070
hear me out until the end.

311
00:22:32,590 --> 00:22:33,950
Beatrice...

312
00:22:34,230 --> 00:22:36,030
Please save me.

313
00:22:36,460 --> 00:22:38,130
H-Huh?

314
00:22:38,260 --> 00:22:41,500
I thought about all kinds 
of cool things to say,

315
00:22:41,500 --> 00:22:44,670
like how I was gonna save 
you from loneliness,

316
00:22:45,100 --> 00:22:49,050
but they all just sounded like stopgaps 
thought up in the heat of the moment.

317
00:22:49,850 --> 00:22:54,930
You don't need me to save you. 
You don't need my help at all.

318
00:22:55,360 --> 00:22:58,850
You're strong, smart, and cute.

319
00:22:59,530 --> 00:23:03,260
You're plenty well-equipped 
to survive on your own.

320
00:23:03,570 --> 00:23:08,700
So saying I'd save you or 
help you out wasn't enough.

321
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:13,160
But even as strong, smart, 
and cute as you are,

322
00:23:13,160 --> 00:23:14,830
you were afraid to live on alone.

323
00:23:15,340 --> 00:23:18,250
You were hurting... and sad, weren't you?

324
00:23:19,010 --> 00:23:24,380
So no one could blame you for clinging 
to the idea of "that person."

325
00:23:25,090 --> 00:23:26,830
Y-You think...

326
00:23:27,140 --> 00:23:30,090
you can just reject how I feel?

327
00:23:31,350 --> 00:23:33,520
What do you know about me?!

328
00:23:37,610 --> 00:23:39,520
I do know you.

329
00:23:39,750 --> 00:23:41,720
I know you're a kind girl.

330
00:23:42,110 --> 00:23:47,800
A girl who'd hold someone's hand and calm 
them when they're wracked by nightmares.

331
00:23:47,800 --> 00:23:49,700
Don't talk as if you know me.

332
00:23:49,700 --> 00:23:53,620
I don't have any strength, 
so I can't be of help to you.

333
00:23:54,250 --> 00:23:58,360
But if there's anything I can do because 
I don't want to leave you alone,

334
00:23:58,920 --> 00:24:01,810
it's to just hang on and keep begging.

335
00:24:09,310 --> 00:24:12,870
Beatrice, please help me.

336
00:24:13,890 --> 00:24:16,800
Without you, I'd be too sad to go on living.

337
00:24:16,800 --> 00:24:17,950
So please help me.

338
00:24:19,900 --> 00:24:21,230
Not fair...

339
00:24:22,900 --> 00:24:26,570
It's not fair... to ask me like that.

340
00:24:27,030 --> 00:24:30,940
You said... that you're not "that person."

341
00:24:31,580 --> 00:24:33,740
You rejected me.

342
00:24:37,500 --> 00:24:38,640
And yet...

343
00:24:39,500 --> 00:24:42,220
I've been alone for 400 years.

344
00:24:43,460 --> 00:24:46,170
Even if I take your hand here and now,

345
00:24:46,170 --> 00:24:48,660
you'll just die soon anyway.

346
00:24:49,390 --> 00:24:54,500
Compared to mine, a human's life 
is over in the blink of an eye.

347
00:24:55,180 --> 00:24:57,600
Clinging to that now wouldn't...

348
00:24:57,600 --> 00:25:02,020
But I'll still be able to 
hold your hand tomorrow.

349
00:25:02,990 --> 00:25:05,770
Tomorrow, and the next day,
 and the day after!

350
00:25:06,690 --> 00:25:08,860
I can't make it 400 years,

351
00:25:08,860 --> 00:25:12,490
but I can spend the days I have with you.

352
00:25:12,820 --> 00:25:15,110
Even if I can't be with you forever,

353
00:25:15,110 --> 00:25:18,870
I can treasure you tomorrow and right now!

354
00:25:20,870 --> 00:25:22,960
So Beatrice...

355
00:25:25,190 --> 00:25:26,920
Choose me.

356
00:25:28,170 --> 00:25:31,130
But... you're not "that person"...

357
00:25:31,130 --> 00:25:32,210
No, I'm not.

358
00:25:32,210 --> 00:25:35,050
I'm me. I'm Natsuki Subaru.

359
00:25:35,050 --> 00:25:39,970
Just forget this crush on some stranger 
you wouldn't even recognize.

360
00:25:41,350 --> 00:25:44,850
Instead of fearing a goodbye 
that might or might not happen,

361
00:25:44,850 --> 00:25:48,650
live with me through a guaranteed 
lifetime of tomorrows!

362
00:25:49,110 --> 00:25:52,900
I'm weak, but I want a lot.

363
00:25:53,320 --> 00:25:57,110
Since you're so caring, 
you'll be so busy looking after me,

364
00:25:57,110 --> 00:26:00,910
you wouldn't have time to think 
about being bored or lonely.

365
00:26:02,870 --> 00:26:05,330
Choose me, Beatrice.

366
00:26:05,710 --> 00:26:08,130
But you'll... go away.

367
00:26:08,130 --> 00:26:09,880
There is no "forever."

368
00:26:09,880 --> 00:26:13,300
The future you're so afraid 
of will come sooner or later.

369
00:26:13,300 --> 00:26:14,210
But still...

370
00:26:14,440 --> 00:26:16,560
You'll leave me.

371
00:26:16,560 --> 00:26:18,420
But still, let's be together!

372
00:26:18,720 --> 00:26:21,760
Let's live together! Let's do things together!

373
00:26:22,140 --> 00:26:24,980
Let's make so many memories 
together that you'll be able

374
00:26:24,980 --> 00:26:27,100
to proudly say you've had fun!

375
00:26:27,560 --> 00:26:32,730
Take back those lonely 400 years 
you've had, with interest!

376
00:26:33,860 --> 00:26:39,880
Even if... I do... you'll 
leave me alone eventually!

377
00:26:40,030 --> 00:26:42,530
For someone like you who'll live forever,

378
00:26:42,530 --> 00:26:46,410
your time with me might 
feel like just a moment.

379
00:26:46,830 --> 00:26:47,580
So...

380
00:26:48,460 --> 00:26:51,090
I'll engrave it all into your soul!

381
00:26:51,880 --> 00:26:53,630
The moment you spend with me,

382
00:26:55,340 --> 00:26:59,430
and the fact that Natsuki Subaru
 was a guy so memorable

383
00:26:59,430 --> 00:27:03,470
that even after an eternity, 
he'll never fade to sepia!

384
00:27:06,930 --> 00:27:09,140
Choose me, Beatrice!

385
00:27:10,810 --> 00:27:13,440
You want someone to get you out of here!

386
00:27:13,440 --> 00:27:17,290
Isn't that why you always sat 
right in front of this door?!

387
00:27:37,760 --> 00:27:39,720
Otto-san, look!

388
00:27:54,730 --> 00:27:55,900
Subaru...

389
00:27:55,900 --> 00:27:57,690
Yeah, that's right.

390
00:27:57,690 --> 00:27:59,660
Subaru... Subaru...

391
00:27:59,860 --> 00:28:01,910
That's right. That's my name.

392
00:28:02,280 --> 00:28:07,120
Subaru! Subaru! Subaru! Subaru!

393
00:28:07,120 --> 00:28:09,080
You finally called me by my name.

394
00:28:19,380 --> 00:28:24,600
I absolutely will not let 
anything or anyone be lost!

395
00:28:27,310 --> 00:28:31,270
Mother and Geuse, everyone from today,

396
00:28:31,810 --> 00:28:35,980
and the words he wrote... 
So long as I remember all of them,

397
00:28:36,360 --> 00:28:38,410
I won't give up!

398
00:28:42,530 --> 00:28:46,620
You don't have to push yourself 
that hard, Emilia-tan.

399
00:28:54,460 --> 00:28:57,920
You can step back and 
leave the rest to me now.

400
00:28:57,920 --> 00:29:00,250
I need to make a revision 
to my first battle.

401
00:29:01,220 --> 00:29:04,480
Sorry... I'm not sure what 
you're talking about.

402
00:29:13,640 --> 00:29:16,690
Don't blame me for whatever may happen next.

403
00:29:16,690 --> 00:29:17,590
Sure.

404
00:29:18,860 --> 00:29:20,850
We'll make it work out!

405
00:29:21,990 --> 00:29:24,450
You and me together!

406
00:29:25,190 --> 00:29:34,260
Choose Me

